<resources>
    <!--
      The legacy launcher background, for the pre-API-26 layer-list icons in mipmap/. API 26+
      uses the adaptive icon in mipmap-anydpi-v26/, whose background is the gradient vector
      @drawable/ic_launcher_background instead — so the two disagree, and this flat indigo is
      what API 24 and 25 actually show.
    -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#4338CA</color>

    <!--
      The window background, which exists before Compose draws anything. It has to match the
      colour the first screen actually paints — the Scaffold's containerColor, which is
      surfaceContainerLowest — or the app opens on a flash of the wrong ground. Kept in step with
      LightSurfaceContainerLowest / DarkSurfaceContainerLowest in ui/theme/Color.kt by hand,
      because an XML theme cannot read a Compose colour.

      With dynamic colour on (the default above API 31) the drawn value comes from the wallpaper
      and may differ slightly. That cannot be helped from here, and it is a near-white or
      near-black either way; the point is to stop inheriting Material's baseline, which is neither.
    -->
    <color name="window_background">#FFFFFFFF</color>
</resources>
